,"score":-1,"flags":3,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"luke8086","user_is_author":false,"tags":["ai","satire"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/nag8vt","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/nag8vt/group_chat_where_your_ai_talks_behind_your"},{"short_id":"mbm7xw","created_at":"2026-11-27T03:11:13.547-06:00","title":"Tiny Hat: a new Linux distro dedicated to retro gamedev","url":"https://roboticoverlords.org/tinyhat","score":30,"flags":0,"comment_count":5,"description":"\u003cp\u003eTiny Hat uses only around 100MB of RAM after booting, and can be booted from a \u0026gt;= 1GB memory stick. It comes with a few small games, an easy way to install and run more games and several example programs for getting into retro game development. It also uses a modern stack of libraries, with dwl / Wayland, SDL3 and GTK4.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne possible use is to buy a cheap x86 machine for younger members of a family, to \u003cdel\u003ecompletely brain wash\u003c/del\u003e inspire them into getting into graphics programming and appreciating retro games, perhaps as a Christmas present.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt least a few people have found it fun so far, so I wanted to share it.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Tiny Hat uses only around 100MB of RAM after booting, and can be booted from a \u003e= 1GB memory stick. It comes with a few small games, an easy way to install and run more games and several example programs for getting into retro game development. It also uses a modern stack of libraries, with dwl / Wayland, SDL3 and GTK4.\r\n\r\nOne possible use is to buy a cheap x86 machine for younger members of a family, to ~~completely brain wash~~ inspire them into getting into graphics programming and appreciating retro games, perhaps as a Christmas present.\r\n\r\nAt least a few people have found it fun so far, so I wanted to share it.","submitter_user":"xyproto","user_is_author":true,"tags":["games","linux","retrocomput